From ec654a1dfe0e55a476cdb035497384b043547e31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AEGIS Platform Team <aegis-ops@localhost>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:01:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] P4 operator fakes + frida argv: survive the noexec engagement
 container (Test-4 round 3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The clean engagement container (compose tmpfs /tmp, noexec by Docker
default) exposed two stacked defects the criterion verdict cannot see:
the harness's operator fakes lived in tempfile.mkdtemp() — on that
noexec /tmp — so os.access(X_OK) failed, shutil.which() silently
skipped them, and the image's REAL frida/mitmdump ran instead of the
fakes; the real frida then rejected the oracle-era --no-pause flag
(current frida-tools auto-resume on spawn and removed it), so every
LIVE frida_hook on the engagement image harvested a usage error —
while the scripted leg still reported rc=0/replay=True/slo=pass (the
criterion verifies capture-window mechanics, not payloads).

Fixes: (1) operator.py drops --no-pause from the frida argv (correct
for every frida the platform rides; ancient CLIs merely harvest a
quieter window); (2) run_exit_criterion.py installs the fakes into the
run scratch (under OUTPUT — the container's exec-allowed evidence
volume) instead of /tmp, and _assert_fakes_runnable refuses LOUDLY on
a non-executable placement instead of silently running the real
binaries; the fakes now persist in --keep evidence for the analyst
record. Reproduced locally (TMPDIR on a noexec tmpfs + a real-frida
mimic on PATH recreated the container's exact [!] harvest) and
verified fixed end-to-end on the same hostile environment.

Regression tests: tests/test_criterion_fakes.py (4: install+run,
loud refusal, PATH shadowing over a real binary, battery contract) +
tests/test_operator_tools.py (1: frida-17-style mimic records argv,
rejects --no-pause, hooks must stream). Full suite 315 -> 320 green.
